cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "pySPLIT: a Python implementation of SPLIT for spatial transcript purification"
message: >-
  If you use pySPLIT, please cite BOTH the original SPLIT paper (which describes
  the method) and this software (which provides the Python implementation).
  The preferred-citation below is the original paper.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Philipp
    family-names: Putze
    email: philipp.putze@tum.de
repository-code: "https://github.com/philinscience/pySPLIT"
abstract: >-
  pySPLIT is a Python implementation of SPLIT (Spatial Purification of Layered
  Intracellular Transcripts) for imaging-based spatial transcriptomics such as
  10x Xenium. It removes transcript spillover between segmented cells using
  deconvolution weights and a single-cell reference, and integrates with the
  scanpy/AnnData ecosystem. The method is described in Bilous et al.,
  Nature Methods (2026); this package reimplements it in Python with a
  sparse-aware purification core and an annotation-method agnostic interface.
keywords:
  - spatial transcriptomics
  - Xenium
  - cell segmentation
  - contamination
  - deconvolution
  - RCTD
  - scanpy
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
